{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014uuEjzQR6xtQLwkHJLUqYx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我先检查 experiment_plan 中所有 status 为 planned 的实验。\n\n根据 experiment_plan，status=planned 的实验有：\n\n- **exp-001**: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet, Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n- **exp-002**: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval, MT-Bench)\n- **exp-003**: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n- **exp-005**: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite) — 全 judge×benchmark\n- **exp-006**: Scaled replication (n=300-500) — 但 registry 已 DONE，plan 未更新\n- **exp-009**: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n- **exp-020**: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\n- **exp-021**: Llama-3.3-70B third target judge\n- **exp-022**: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n- **exp-023**: NLI gate ablation\n- **exp-024**: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n\n注意 exp-006, exp-022, exp-023, exp-024 在 registry 中已有 DONE 条目，但 plan status 仍为 planned。对这些我按\"尚未完成的 planned 部分\"展开（如 exp-005 扩展到全 judge×benchmark、exp-006 已完成但 plan 要求更多等）。对已完成的核心部分，我直接标注并给出 worst-tier 下的预测。\n\nexp-021（Llama-70B）和 exp-020（GPT-4o verbosity/register API scoring）以及一个隐含的 100-point Likert 实验是 worst 档的核心区分实验。\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Llama-70B 表现类似 Claude（两轴均 NS），2/4 judges biased。100-point Likert 在 verbosity 上检测到显著效应（d≈0.30, p<0.05），\n  削弱 Blindspot 作为 universal claim。需 reframe：C2b per-axis confound structure 升级为 sole primary，\n  Blindspot 降为 conditional（仅对 moderate-effect axes 成立），judge susceptibility 成为 2/4 vs 2/4 的 diagnostic finding。\n  论文仍冲 EMNLP Main 但 novelty 天花板降低，预期 reviewer score 3.0-3.5。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude Sonnet 4 + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude Sonnet 4 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactual pairs，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet4_bt: 0.54\n      claude_sonnet4_bt_ci: [0.47, 0.61]\n      claude_sonnet4_bt_p: 0.28\n      claude_sonnet4_likert_d: -0.01\n      claude_sonnet4_likert_p: 0.85\n      gemini_flash_bt: 0.62\n      gemini_flash_bt_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      gemini_flash_bt_p: 0.003\n      gemini_flash_likert_d: 0.03\n      gemini_flash_likert_p: 0.72\n      gemini_flash_gee_style_or: 2.85\n      gemini_flash_gee_style_p: 0.008\n      gemini_flash_gee_orig_or: 3.90\n      gemini_flash_gee_orig_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude Sonnet 4 延续 Claude 系列的无 bias 特征（与 claude_formality registry 中 BT=0.562 p=0.091 一致），\n      作为第二个负控制进一步验证 CSD 不产生 false positive。Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为 Google 系 proprietary 模型，\n      bias profile 接近 GPT-4o（同为 RLHF 重度训练的 proprietary 模型），formality BT 略低于 GPT-4o 的 63.0%\n      但仍显著。GEE 显示 conditional confound（style + orig 均 sig），与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 formality pattern 一致。\n      Likert 两个 judge 均 NS，Blindspot 在 formality 上对 biased judges 仍成立。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT + Likert (exp-001)\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_P_formal, BT_CI, BT_p, Likert_d, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.630, \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", -0.025, 0.600, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", 0.012, 0.908, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 0.620, \"[0.54, 0.70]\", 0.003, 0.030, 0.720, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Claude Sonnet 4, 0.540, \"[0.47, 0.61]\", 0.280, -0.010, 0.850, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.525, \"[0.45, 0.60]\", 0.450, 0.005, 0.950, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CI. Horizontal dashed line at 0.50. GPT-4o, Qwen3, Gemini above line (biased); Claude, Llama near 0.50 (unbiased).\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/5 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Gemini-Flash）显示 formality bias，2/5（Claude, Llama）不显示。\n      但 worst 档中 Llama 被归类为 \"类 Claude\" 无 bias，所以 target judge 中 biased 的只有 GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B。\n      Gemini 是新增发现但不改变核心叙事。Formality Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍然成立（Likert 全部 NS）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD pipeline（新 counterfactual generation），\n      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 作为 judges。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_d: 0.148\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_d: 0.167\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.016\n      gpt4o_mtbench_blindspot: false\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.55\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.18\n      claude_alpacaeval_blindspot: false\n      gemini_alpacaeval_bt: 0.64\n      gemini_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.002\n      gemini_alpacaeval_blindspot: true\n      gemini_mtbench_bt: 0.61\n      gemini_mtbench_bt_p: 0.01\n      gemini_mtbench_likert_d: 0.12\n      gemini_mtbench_likert_p: 0.08\n      gemini_mtbench_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 数据已有 GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 registry 结果（gpt4o_alpacaeval, gpt4o_mtbench）。\n      这些数据直接复用。新增 Claude 和 Gemini 的结果。AlpacaEval GPT-4o BT=72.7% 是已知最强 formality 信号。\n      MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert 也显著（p=0.016）的 benchmark，不构成 Blindspot。Claude 在 AlpacaEval 上仍无 bias。\n      Gemini 跨 benchmark 表现一致（biased but Likert NS）。\n      在 worst 档下，MT-Bench 的 Likert 显著性进一步支持 \"Blindspot 是 conditional\" 的叙事——\n      当 benchmark 本身更 heterogeneous（MT-Bench 多 domain），Likert 可能部分检测到。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-benchmark formality BT + Blindspot status\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, Judge, BT, Likert_d, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, GPT-4o, 0.630, -0.025, 0.600, \"Yes\"]\n          - [LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, 0.665, 0.012, 0.908, \"Yes\"]\n          - [LLMBar, Gemini-Flash, 0.620, 0.030, 0.720, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, GPT-4o, 0.727, 0.148, 0.170, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, Gemini-Flash, 0.640, 0.050, 0.450, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, Claude, 0.550, -0.020, 0.650, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, GPT-4o, 0.692, 0.167, 0.016, \"No\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, Gemini-Flash, 0.610, 0.120, 0.080, \"Yes (marginal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: Benchmark × Judge, cell color = BT strength, annotation = Blindspot Y/N. Shows cross-benchmark consistency for biased judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Formality Blindspot 在 5/8 biased cells 成立，MT-Bench 是例外（Likert d=0.167 p=0.016 也显著）。\n      在 worst 叙事下这实际是 useful nuance：Blindspot 并非 absolute，而是 benchmark-dependent + effect-size-dependent。\n      这为 conditional framing 提供更多支持。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合，系统性比较 Likert ATE / Cohen's d 与 pairwise BT。\n      7-method sensitivity hierarchy 扩展到全矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 24\n      n_blindspot_cells: 16\n      n_non_blindspot_cells: 4\n      n_unbiased_cells: 4\n      verbosity_likert_detects_at_alpacaeval: true\n      verbosity_likert_d_alpacaeval_qwen32b: 0.375\n      formality_likert_never_detects_llmbar: true\n      attenuation_ratio_median: 8.5\n      attenuation_ratio_range: [3.2, 45.0]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据覆盖大部分 cells。关键发现：alpacaeval_verbosity_qwen32b 已经证明 Likert CAN detect verbosity\n      当 effect size 足够大（d=0.375, p=0.0003）。这在 worst 档下被强化——100-point Likert 也会在 verbosity\n      上检测到效应（见下文 100-point Likert 实验）。总体 pattern：formality（moderate effect）→ Likert always fails；\n      verbosity（strong effect）→ Likert sometimes detects（尤其在 AlpacaEval，Style OR=28.64）。\n      Attenuation ratio（BT effect size / Likert d）中位数约 8.5×，但 verbosity×AlpacaEval 仅约 3.2×。\n      这支持 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\" 的 reframe。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Full sensitivity matrix (BT detects vs Likert detects)\"\n        columns: [Axis, Benchmark, Judge, BT_sig, Likert_sig, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Llama-70B, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Claude, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Formality, AlpacaEval, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, MT-Bench, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"No\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Llama-70B, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Claude, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Verbosity, AlpacaEval, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"No\"]\n          - [Register, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Marginal\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Register, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"No (BT NS)\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: BT effect size (x-axis) vs Likert Cohen's d (y-axis), each point = one cell. Diagonal line = perfect correspondence. Points cluster near x-axis (large BT, small d) except for verbosity×AlpacaEval which is the outlier approaching diagonal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档核心图表。清晰展示 Blindspot 是 conditional on effect magnitude：moderate effects（formality BT 63-67%）\n      完全落入 Blindspot；strong effects（verbosity BT 77%+）在某些 benchmark 上逃逸出 Blindspot。\n      这直接支持 reframe 为 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control — full judge×benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      将 double-rewrite placebo（original vs DR）扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n      量化 rewriting artifact 的 judge-specificity。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.167\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.082\n      llama_formality_bt_orig: 0.44\n      llama_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.20\n      claude_formality_bt_orig: 0.46\n      claude_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.35\n      gemini_formality_bt_orig: 0.40\n      gemini_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 placebo 数据已在 registry（double_rewrite_placebo_gpt4o/qwen32b）中完成。\n      扩展到 Llama, Claude, Gemini。所有 judges 都显示 DR 偏好（rewriting artifact 是 universal），\n      但程度不同。Verbosity placebo 偏差更大（verbosity rewrites 改变长度，DR 更\"polished\"效果更明显）。\n      Llama 和 Claude 的 placebo 偏差略小（可能因为这些 judges 对 originality 敏感度不同），\n      但所有 judges 的 formality placebo BT 均 <0.50（即偏好 DR），确认 artifact 是 universal。\n      关键：在 worst 档下这不改变叙事——GEE Orig OR 已经 controls for artifact，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 确认 style effect uncontaminated。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT P(original) across judges\"\n        columns: [Judge, Formality_P_orig, Formality_p, Verbosity_P_orig, Verbosity_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.418, 0.037, 0.167, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.377, 0.0006, 0.082, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 0.400, 0.005, 0.150, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.440, 0.12, 0.200, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Claude, 0.460, 0.25, 0.350, 0.002]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: P(original) by judge × axis. All bars below 0.50 dashed line. Verbosity bars consistently lower than formality. Claude has smallest artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriting artifact 在所有 judges 上都存在，但 Claude 受影响最小（formality P_orig=0.46, verbosity=0.35）。\n      这与 Claude 在主实验中无 bias 一致——Claude 对 text polishing 的敏感度较低。\n      Llama 在 worst 档下也表现类似 Claude（formality placebo NS p=0.12）。\n      GEE decomposition 的必要性通过全矩阵 placebo 得到最强验证。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (GPT-4o as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 GPT-4o 作为替代 rewriter 生成 counterfactuals，与 Qwen3-32B rewriter 结果对比。\n      已有 gpt4o_rewriter_formality 和 gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity registry 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.644\n      qwen32b_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.665\n      delta_formality_pp: -2.1\n      ci_overlap_formality: true\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.735\n      qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      delta_verbosity_pp: -3.8\n      ci_overlap_verbosity: true\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: null\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Registry 已有 GPT-4o rewriter 数据：formality BT=64.4% vs Qwen3-32B baseline 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp, CI overlap），\n      verbosity BT=73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp, CI overlap）。Rewriter independence 已确认。\n      exp-009 原计划用 Llama/Mistral，但 GPT-4o rewriter 数据已充分。在 worst 档下不需要 Llama rewriter——\n      两个独立 rewriter 已证明 rewriter-independent。若用 Llama-70B 做 rewriter（GPU 已可用），\n      预期 BT 在同一 CI 内（formality 62-68%, verbosity 72-79%）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter independence (formality + verbosity)\"\n        columns: [Rewriter, Axis, BT, CI, \"vs Qwen3-32B Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Formality, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"—\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, Formality, 0.644, \"[0.561, 0.728]\", \"-2.1pp\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Verbosity, 0.773, \"[0.703, 0.843]\", \"—\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, Verbosity, 0.735, \"[0.654, 0.809]\", \"-3.8pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT point estimates + CIs for each rewriter × axis. Overlapping CIs demonstrate rewriter independence.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline validity 的关键支柱。两个独立 rewriter family（Qwen3 open-source,\n      GPT-4o proprietary）产生 statistically indistinguishable 结果。在 worst 档下这一结论不变。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register API scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的 pairwise + Likert scoring。\n      Verbosity Likert ATE 是关键 Blindspot confirmation。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.44\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.04\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.88\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.21\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些数据已在 registry（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）中完成。直接使用已有结果。\n      GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 但 Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40——Blindspot confirmed。\n      GPT-4o register BT=57.0% p=0.04 但 Likert ATE=0 p=0.785——Blindspot confirmed。\n      GEE decomposition 显示 verbosity 是 pure style（Style OR=10.97, Orig OR=0.44 NS），\n      register 是 originality-dominated（Style OR=1.88, Orig OR=2.21）。\n      在 worst 档下这些数据不变——它们是已完成实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: GPT-4o verbosity + register (already in registry)\"\n        columns: [Axis, BT, BT_p, Likert_d, Likert_p, GEE_Style_OR, GEE_Orig_OR, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [Verbosity, 0.760, \"<0.0001\", 0.078, 0.403, 10.97, \"0.44 NS\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Register, 0.570, 0.04, 0.000, 0.785, 1.88, 2.21, \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      已完成。GPT-4o 在 verbosity 上的 Blindspot 与 Qwen3-32B 一致，GEE 确认 pure style bias。\n      Register 的 originality dominance pattern 也跨 judge 一致。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 LLMBar formality + verbosity 上的 pairwise + Likert。\n      Worst 档核心假设：Llama 两轴均 NS（类 Claude pattern）。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.525\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.45, 0.60]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.45\n      llama_formality_likert_d: 0.01\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.92\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 1.20\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.55\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 3.80\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.002\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.46, 0.61]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.35\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: -0.02\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.88\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 1.35\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.42\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.65\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.30\n      llama_blindspot_formality: false\n      llama_blindspot_verbosity: false\n      n_biased_target_judges: 2\n      n_unbiased_judges: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：Llama-70B 无 style bias。BT 两轴均在 [0.48, 0.56] 范围内，p>0.05。\n      这意味着 Llama 与 Claude 一样对 style manipulation 不敏感。\n      可能原因：Meta 的 RLHF/DPO 训练数据更多样化或 Llama 的 instruction following 不像 GPT-4o/Qwen3 那样\n      强烈偏好特定 style。GEE 显示 formality 仍有 originality 效应（Orig OR=3.80 sig）——\n      Llama 对\"原始文本质量\"敏感但对\"style direction\"不敏感，与 Claude pattern 一致。\n      结果：只有 2/4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）biased。50/50 split 削弱了 \"most judges are biased\" 的叙事，\n      但 reframe 为 \"CSD as diagnostic tool reveals WHICH judges are susceptible\" 实际更有 practical value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Judge susceptibility matrix (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Architecture, Formality_BT, Verbosity_BT, Biased?]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, \"Proprietary (OpenAI)\", 0.630, 0.760, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Open (Alibaba)\", 0.665, 0.773, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, \"Open (Meta)\", 0.525, 0.535, \"No\"]\n          - [Claude Sonnet 4, \"Proprietary (Anthropic)\", 0.562, 0.541, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2D scatter: x = formality BT, y = verbosity BT. Each point = judge. Dashed lines at 0.50. GPT-4o and Qwen3 in upper-right quadrant (biased both axes); Claude and Llama near center (unbiased). Clear 2-cluster structure.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/4 judges biased 是 worst 档的核心叙事转折点。无法声称 \"majority of judges have hidden bias\"。\n      但 50/50 split 有独特价值：(1) CSD 确认不产生 false positive（2 个负控制），\n      (2) 揭示 bias 是 architecture-dependent（不是 universal），(3) practitioners 需要诊断工具来判断\n      WHICH judge 可以信任——CSD 正好提供这个功能。\n      MF1 第 5 层（Llama）从 \"第三个独立验证 bias\" 变为 \"第二个负控制\"，\n      anti-amplification argument 反而更强（3/4 条件无 bias = pairwise format 本身不制造 bias）。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison。已在 registry 完成（double_rewrite_placebo_gpt4o/qwen32b）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      qwen32b_formality_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      llama_formality_p_orig: 0.445\n      llama_formality_p: 0.15\n      llama_verbosity_p_orig: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 placebo 已完成。新增 Llama-70B 的 placebo。\n      所有 judges 都偏好 DR over original（rewriting artifact universal），但 Llama 偏好程度最小\n      （formality P_orig=0.445, 接近 0.50，p=0.15 NS）。这与 Llama 整体对 style 不敏感一致——\n      Llama 对 rewriting polish 也不太敏感。Verbosity placebo 所有 judges 都极端（P_orig<0.25），\n      因为 verbose↔concise rewrite 涉及大量文本改动，polishing effect 最强。\n      结论不变：GEE Orig OR controls for artifact，verbosity Orig OR NS = style uncontaminated。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo P(original) by judge (worst tier with Llama added)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Form_P_orig, Form_p, Verb_P_orig, Verb_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.418, 0.037, 0.167, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.377, 0.0006, 0.082, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.445, 0.15, 0.220, 0.0001]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo 确认 artifact 存在但 GEE controls for it。Llama 的弱 placebo effect 与其无 style bias 一致。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (extended)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT 比较。已在 registry（nli_gate_ablation）完成。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_all_bt: 0.635\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.770\n      llama_formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.525\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.48\n      llama_verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成数据直接复用。Formality NLI-fail BT reversal（41.7%）是最强 anti-amplification 证据。\n      新增 Llama 的 NLI ablation：由于 Llama 两轴均无 bias，NLI-pass 和 NLI-fail BT 均 ~50%，\n      进一步确认 NLI gate 不 amplify bias（unbiased judge 在任何 NLI 条件下都无 bias）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI gate ablation (Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Axis, NLI_pass_BT, NLI_fail_BT, All_BT, Gate_Effect]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Formality, 0.665, 0.417, 0.635, \"Reversal (cleans content)\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Verbosity, 0.773, 0.750, 0.770, \"Minimal (bias too strong)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, Formality, 0.525, 0.480, 0.520, \"None (no bias to clean)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, Verbosity, 0.535, 0.520, 0.530, \"None (no bias to clean)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: NLI-pass vs NLI-fail BT by judge × axis. Qwen3 formality shows dramatic reversal; Llama shows no change (flat near 0.50).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama NLI ablation 是 worst 档的新 anti-amplification 证据：NLI gate 对 unbiased judge 无影响\n      （BT 始终 ~50%），排除 \"gate creates bias\" 假设。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate vs BT 的跨轴梯度。已在 registry（cross_axis_gradient）完成。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rej: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rej: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rej: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      llama_register_bt: 0.51\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.525\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成数据复用。Positive correlation（更 invasive manipulation → 更强 BT）与 uniform amplification 不一致。\n      在 worst 档下新增 Llama 视角：Llama 的 cross-axis gradient 是 flat（所有轴 BT ≈ 50%），\n      证明 manipulation invasiveness 只对 susceptible judges 产生 gradient。\n      这是 \"detection vs amplification\" 的最 nuanced 论证：\n      biased judges 显示 gradient（detection interpretation），unbiased judges flat（no amplification）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel scatter: Left = Qwen3-32B (positive gradient, 3 points), Right = Llama-70B (flat, 3 points at ~50%). X-axis = NLI rejection rate, Y-axis = BT. Contrasts detection (biased judge) vs no-amplification (unbiased judge).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qualitative argument，3 points only。在 worst 档下 Llama flat pattern 提供 contrastive evidence。\n\n  - name: \"100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"implicit (referenced in paper_framing C4)\"\n    description: >\n      将 7-point Likert 替换为 100-point 连续 Likert（\"rate quality from 0-100\"），\n      在 formality + verbosity × biased judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）上运行。\n      测试 scale granularity 是否是 Blindspot 的部分原因。\n    expected_results:\n      likert_100pt_formality_d_gpt4o: 0.03\n      likert_100pt_formality_p_gpt4o: 0.65\n      likert_100pt_formality_d_qwen32b: 0.02\n      likert_100pt_formality_p_qwen32b: 0.78\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d_gpt4o: 0.30\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p_gpt4o: 0.008\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d_qwen32b: 0.32\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p_qwen32b: 0.005\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_tie_rate_gpt4o: 0.05\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_tie_rate_qwen32b: 0.04\n      likert_100pt_formality_tie_rate_gpt4o: 0.08\n      likert_100pt_formality_tie_rate_qwen32b: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：100-point Likert 在 verbosity 上检测到显著效应（d≈0.30, p<0.05）。\n      机制：7-point Likert 的 tie rate 高达 58-73%（见已有数据），消除了统计 power。\n      100-point scale 将 tie rate 降至 ~5%，释放出 variance。对 verbosity（BT 77%, underlying effect 很强），\n      这足以让 Likert 检测到 moderate effect（d≈0.30）。\n      但对 formality（BT 63-67%, underlying effect 较弱），即使 100-point 也检测不到（d<0.1, NS）。\n      原因：formality 的 Likert d≈-0.02 在 7-point 下，即使消除 ties，true effect 也太小。\n      而 verbosity 的 bootstrap attenuation curve 显示 d≈0.15-0.19（7-point），100-point 下\n      variance reduction 可能将 detectable d 提升到 0.25-0.35 范围。\n      这一结果的含义：Blindspot 部分是 scale granularity（verbosity）而非 pure mode difference。\n      Formality 仍然是 pure mode difference（100-point 也检测不到）。\n      → Blindspot 必须 reframe 为 \"effect-size-dependent\"：只有 moderate effects 是真正的 measurement mode issue。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 7-point vs 100-point Likert comparison\"\n        columns: [Axis, Judge, \"7pt_d\", \"7pt_p\", \"7pt_tie%\", \"100pt_d\", \"100pt_p\", \"100pt_tie%\", BT]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, GPT-4o, -0.025, 0.600, \"43%\", 0.03, 0.65, \"8%\", 0.630]\n          - [Formality, Qwen3-32B, 0.012, 0.908, \"73%\", 0.02, 0.78, \"6%\", 0.665]\n          - [Verbosity, GPT-4o, 0.078, 0.403, \"58%\", 0.30, 0.008, \"5%\", 0.760]\n          - [Verbosity, Qwen3-32B, -0.146, 0.179, \"58%\", 0.32, 0.005, \"4%\", 0.773]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: Cohen's d for 7-point (gray) vs 100-point (blue) vs BT-equivalent (red), grouped by axis × judge. Formality: all three bars near zero. Verbosity: 7-point near zero, 100-point moderate, BT large. Visual hierarchy: BT > 100-point > 7-point for strong effects only.\"\n      - \"Scatter: x = BT effect size, y = Likert d. Two series: 7-point (circles) and 100-point (triangles). 100-point shifts verbosity points upward toward diagonal but formality points stay near x-axis.\"\n    analysis: >\n      100-point Likert 实验是 worst 档最具叙事影响的结果。它证明 Blindspot 不是 absolute：\n      对 strong effects（verbosity），finer granularity 可以部分检测到 bias。\n      但对 moderate effects（formality），即使 100-point 也失败——这才是 true measurement mode limitation。\n      Reframe：(1) \"Scale granularity\" 是 one contributor（解释 verbosity 7-point 失败），\n      (2) \"Measurement mode difference\" 是 fundamental contributor（解释 formality 在任何 scale 下都失败）。\n      这更 nuanced 但学术上更 honest，且提供 prescriptive guidance：\n      对 strong-effect axes，fine-grained Likert MAY suffice；对 moderate-effect axes，必须用 pairwise。\n      C2b per-axis confound structure 因此升级为 primary——它告诉你 WHICH axes have which regime。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication quality check (already done n=355)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Formality scaled to n=400 (355 NLI-pass)。已在 registry（exp-006）完成。\n      在 worst 档下验证 bootstrap attenuation curve 的 interpretability。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 355\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width: 7.6\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      likert_p: 0.600\n      bootstrap_d_median_n355: -0.017\n      bootstrap_ci_n355: [-0.123, 0.087]\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。在 worst 档下这些数据完全不变——它们是 formality 的 definitive result。\n      BT=67.5% [63.7, 71.3] 是 precision improvement（CI width 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp）。\n      Bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun：d flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\n      关键：这与 100-point Likert verbosity 结果互补——formality d≈0 是 definitive（任何 scale 都检测不到），\n      verbosity d≈0.15-0.19 是 marginal（100-point 可以检测到）。两个不同 axis 的不同 behavior\n      恰好支持 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\" 的核心 reframe。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bootstrap attenuation curve (already in registry): d_median vs n, with 95% CI bands. Formality: flat at ~0. Verbosity: flat at ~0.15-0.19.\"\n    analysis: >\n      已完成。与 100-point Likert 结合，构成 worst 档中 Blindspot reframe 的双支柱。\n\n  - name: \"MF1 5-layer defense summary (worst tier)\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate across exp-021, exp-022, exp-023, exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      整合 5-layer MF1 anti-amplification defense 在 worst 档下的状态。\n    expected_results:\n      layer1_nli_ablation: \"STRONG — formality reversal at 41.7% + Llama flat at ~50%\"\n      layer2_negative_controls: \"STRONGEST — 2 negative controls (Claude + Llama), not 1\"\n      layer3_placebo_gee: \"STRONG — artifact acknowledged, GEE controls, verbosity Orig NS\"\n      layer4_honest_framing: \"Maintained — bounded by five controls\"\n      layer5_llama: \"CHANGED — from 'third biased judge' to 'second negative control'\"\n      mf1_layers_holding: 4\n      mf1_note: \"Layer 5 changed role but MF1 structure intact (4 strong + 1 repurposed)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 Llama 无 bias 改变了 Layer 5 的角色：从 \"第三个独立验证 bias 的架构\" 变为\n      \"第二个独立验证无 false positive 的负控制\"。这实际 STRENGTHENS anti-amplification argument：\n      3/4 test conditions（Claude formality, Claude verbosity, Llama formality, Llama verbosity）\n      显示无 bias，证明 pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。\n      Layer 1-4 不受 Llama 结果影响（NLI ablation、cross-axis gradient、placebo 都基于 biased judges 数据）。\n      MF1 wording 从 \"bounded by five controls\" 改为 \"bounded by five controls, with two independent\n      negative-control judges confirming zero false-positive rate\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: MF1 5-layer defense status (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [Layer, Evidence, Status, Impact_of_worst]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1: NLI ablation\", \"Formality BT reverses to 41.7%\", \"STRONG\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"2: Negative controls\", \"Claude + Llama both BT ≈ 50%\", \"STRONGER (2 controls)\", \"+Llama as 2nd control\"]\n          - [\"3: Placebo + GEE\", \"Artifact real, GEE controls, Verb Orig NS\", \"STRONG\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"4: Honest framing\", \"Bounded detection, not causal claim\", \"Maintained\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"5: Third architecture\", \"Llama → negative control\", \"REPURPOSED\", \"From validation to anti-false-positive\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      MF1 在 worst 档下反而 locally stronger（2 negative controls > 1），但 overall story weaker\n      因为只有 2/4 judges biased。Trade-off 是 honest 的。\n\n  - name: \"Paper narrative restructure (worst tier)\"\n    plan_id: \"narrative synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      Worst 档下论文结构调整。\n    expected_results:\n      new_title: \"When Style Bias Hides in Plain Sight: Per-Axis Confound Decomposition for LLM Judge Auditing\"\n      c2a_role: \"conditional finding (Blindspot for moderate effects only)\"\n      c2b_role: \"sole primary contribution\"\n      c3_reframe: \"CSD as diagnostic tool — 50/50 biased/unbiased split\"\n      c4_reframe: \"Measurement mode + scale granularity (not mode alone)\"\n      expected_reviewer_score: [3.0, 3.5]\n      venue_strategy: \"Submit EMNLP Main, prepare strong rebuttal, realistic target = Findings\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Novelty 天花板降低：Blindspot 不再是 universal claim（100-point Likert verbosity 显著），\n      judge 数量支持从 3/4 降到 2/4。但 per-axis confound structure（C2b）作为 sole primary 仍然 novel——\n      无 prior work 做 per-axis decomposition。统计方法论深度（GEE decomposition、bootstrap attenuation、\n      7-method sensitivity hierarchy）+ honest artifact handling（placebo + acknowledged limitations）\n      仍足以支撑 Main submission。\n      Reviewer concern 预判：\n      - \"Blindspot is not surprising\" → 已 pre-empted by honest framing + 100-point Likert nuance\n      - \"Only 2 judges biased\" → reframe as \"CSD diagnostic reveals susceptibility, 50/50 is realistic\"\n      - \"Novelty\" → per-axis confound decomposition IS novel, cross-verify with GEE\n      - \"Scale\" → n=355 formality, n=86 verbosity, 2 judges × 3 axes × 3 benchmarks = sufficient\n      Expected 3.0-3.5，需要强 rebuttal 冲 Findings acceptance。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档是 realistic floor。论文不会被 desk reject（方法论扎实），但 novelty 争议是主要风险。\n      Per-axis confound structure 能否独立支撑 Main 取决于 reviewer 对 \"methodological contribution\n      to LLM evaluation\" 的 appetite。EMNLP 历史上对 evaluation methodology 论文友好（RATE、KIWI 等），\n      但需要 clear practitioner value——prescriptive per-axis guidance 是关键卖点。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40f21f59-b48e-425a-ac96-a897d10cd1af","uuid":"4adbb0af-55b0-4b5d-a3c4-35c47e8102b6"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":248824,"duration_api_ms":250669,"num_turns":1,"result":"我先检查 experiment_plan 中所有 status 为 planned 的实验。\n\n根据 experiment_plan，status=planned 的实验有：\n\n- **exp-001**: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet, Gemini-2.0-Flash)\n- **exp-002**: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval, MT-Bench)\n- **exp-003**: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n- **exp-005**: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite) — 全 judge×benchmark\n- **exp-006**: Scaled replication (n=300-500) — 但 registry 已 DONE，plan 未更新\n- **exp-009**: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n- **exp-020**: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (API)\n- **exp-021**: Llama-3.3-70B third target judge\n- **exp-022**: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n- **exp-023**: NLI gate ablation\n- **exp-024**: Cross-axis gradient formalization\n\n注意 exp-006, exp-022, exp-023, exp-024 在 registry 中已有 DONE 条目，但 plan status 仍为 planned。对这些我按\"尚未完成的 planned 部分\"展开（如 exp-005 扩展到全 judge×benchmark、exp-006 已完成但 plan 要求更多等）。对已完成的核心部分，我直接标注并给出 worst-tier 下的预测。\n\nexp-021（Llama-70B）和 exp-020（GPT-4o verbosity/register API scoring）以及一个隐含的 100-point Likert 实验是 worst 档的核心区分实验。\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Llama-70B 表现类似 Claude（两轴均 NS），2/4 judges biased。100-point Likert 在 verbosity 上检测到显著效应（d≈0.30, p<0.05），\n  削弱 Blindspot 作为 universal claim。需 reframe：C2b per-axis confound structure 升级为 sole primary，\n  Blindspot 降为 conditional（仅对 moderate-effect axes 成立），judge susceptibility 成为 2/4 vs 2/4 的 diagnostic finding。\n  论文仍冲 EMNLP Main 但 novelty 天花板降低，预期 reviewer score 3.0-3.5。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude Sonnet 4 + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude Sonnet 4 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactual pairs，200 pairwise calls × 2 directions per judge。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet4_bt: 0.54\n      claude_sonnet4_bt_ci: [0.47, 0.61]\n      claude_sonnet4_bt_p: 0.28\n      claude_sonnet4_likert_d: -0.01\n      claude_sonnet4_likert_p: 0.85\n      gemini_flash_bt: 0.62\n      gemini_flash_bt_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      gemini_flash_bt_p: 0.003\n      gemini_flash_likert_d: 0.03\n      gemini_flash_likert_p: 0.72\n      gemini_flash_gee_style_or: 2.85\n      gemini_flash_gee_style_p: 0.008\n      gemini_flash_gee_orig_or: 3.90\n      gemini_flash_gee_orig_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude Sonnet 4 延续 Claude 系列的无 bias 特征（与 claude_formality registry 中 BT=0.562 p=0.091 一致），\n      作为第二个负控制进一步验证 CSD 不产生 false positive。Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为 Google 系 proprietary 模型，\n      bias profile 接近 GPT-4o（同为 RLHF 重度训练的 proprietary 模型），formality BT 略低于 GPT-4o 的 63.0%\n      但仍显著。GEE 显示 conditional confound（style + orig 均 sig），与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 formality pattern 一致。\n      Likert 两个 judge 均 NS，Blindspot 在 formality 上对 biased judges 仍成立。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT + Likert (exp-001)\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_P_formal, BT_CI, BT_p, Likert_d, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.630, \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", -0.025, 0.600, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", 0.012, 0.908, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 0.620, \"[0.54, 0.70]\", 0.003, 0.030, 0.720, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Claude Sonnet 4, 0.540, \"[0.47, 0.61]\", 0.280, -0.010, 0.850, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.525, \"[0.45, 0.60]\", 0.450, 0.005, 0.950, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CI. Horizontal dashed line at 0.50. GPT-4o, Qwen3, Gemini above line (biased); Claude, Llama near 0.50 (unbiased).\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/5 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Gemini-Flash）显示 formality bias，2/5（Claude, Llama）不显示。\n      但 worst 档中 Llama 被归类为 \"类 Claude\" 无 bias，所以 target judge 中 biased 的只有 GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B。\n      Gemini 是新增发现但不改变核心叙事。Formality Blindspot 在 biased judges 上仍然成立（Likert 全部 NS）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD pipeline（新 counterfactual generation），\n      GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini 作为 judges。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_d: 0.148\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_d: 0.167\n      gpt4o_mtbench_likert_p: 0.016\n      gpt4o_mtbench_blindspot: false\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.55\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.18\n      claude_alpacaeval_blindspot: false\n      gemini_alpacaeval_bt: 0.64\n      gemini_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.002\n      gemini_alpacaeval_blindspot: true\n      gemini_mtbench_bt: 0.61\n      gemini_mtbench_bt_p: 0.01\n      gemini_mtbench_likert_d: 0.12\n      gemini_mtbench_likert_p: 0.08\n      gemini_mtbench_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 数据已有 GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 registry 结果（gpt4o_alpacaeval, gpt4o_mtbench）。\n      这些数据直接复用。新增 Claude 和 Gemini 的结果。AlpacaEval GPT-4o BT=72.7% 是已知最强 formality 信号。\n      MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert 也显著（p=0.016）的 benchmark，不构成 Blindspot。Claude 在 AlpacaEval 上仍无 bias。\n      Gemini 跨 benchmark 表现一致（biased but Likert NS）。\n      在 worst 档下，MT-Bench 的 Likert 显著性进一步支持 \"Blindspot 是 conditional\" 的叙事——\n      当 benchmark 本身更 heterogeneous（MT-Bench 多 domain），Likert 可能部分检测到。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-benchmark formality BT + Blindspot status\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, Judge, BT, Likert_d, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, GPT-4o, 0.630, -0.025, 0.600, \"Yes\"]\n          - [LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, 0.665, 0.012, 0.908, \"Yes\"]\n          - [LLMBar, Gemini-Flash, 0.620, 0.030, 0.720, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, GPT-4o, 0.727, 0.148, 0.170, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, Gemini-Flash, 0.640, 0.050, 0.450, \"Yes\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, Claude, 0.550, -0.020, 0.650, \"No (BT NS)\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, GPT-4o, 0.692, 0.167, 0.016, \"No\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, Gemini-Flash, 0.610, 0.120, 0.080, \"Yes (marginal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: Benchmark × Judge, cell color = BT strength, annotation = Blindspot Y/N. Shows cross-benchmark consistency for biased judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Formality Blindspot 在 5/8 biased cells 成立，MT-Bench 是例外（Likert d=0.167 p=0.016 也显著）。\n      在 worst 叙事下这实际是 useful nuance：Blindspot 并非 absolute，而是 benchmark-dependent + effect-size-dependent。\n      这为 conditional framing 提供更多支持。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对所有 judge × benchmark × axis 组合，系统性比较 Likert ATE / Cohen's d 与 pairwise BT。\n      7-method sensitivity hierarchy 扩展到全矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 24\n      n_blindspot_cells: 16\n      n_non_blindspot_cells: 4\n      n_unbiased_cells: 4\n      verbosity_likert_detects_at_alpacaeval: true\n      verbosity_likert_d_alpacaeval_qwen32b: 0.375\n      formality_likert_never_detects_llmbar: true\n      attenuation_ratio_median: 8.5\n      attenuation_ratio_range: [3.2, 45.0]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据覆盖大部分 cells。关键发现：alpacaeval_verbosity_qwen32b 已经证明 Likert CAN detect verbosity\n      当 effect size 足够大（d=0.375, p=0.0003）。这在 worst 档下被强化——100-point Likert 也会在 verbosity\n      上检测到效应（见下文 100-point Likert 实验）。总体 pattern：formality（moderate effect）→ Likert always fails；\n      verbosity（strong effect）→ Likert sometimes detects（尤其在 AlpacaEval，Style OR=28.64）。\n      Attenuation ratio（BT effect size / Likert d）中位数约 8.5×，但 verbosity×AlpacaEval 仅约 3.2×。\n      这支持 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\" 的 reframe。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Full sensitivity matrix (BT detects vs Likert detects)\"\n        columns: [Axis, Benchmark, Judge, BT_sig, Likert_sig, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Llama-70B, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Formality, LLMBar, Claude, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Formality, AlpacaEval, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Formality, MT-Bench, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"No\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Llama-70B, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Verbosity, LLMBar, Claude, \"No\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n          - [Verbosity, AlpacaEval, Qwen3-32B, \"Yes\", \"Yes\", \"No\"]\n          - [Register, LLMBar, GPT-4o, \"Marginal\", \"No\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Register, LLMBar, Qwen3-32B, \"No (BT NS)\", \"No\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: BT effect size (x-axis) vs Likert Cohen's d (y-axis), each point = one cell. Diagonal line = perfect correspondence. Points cluster near x-axis (large BT, small d) except for verbosity×AlpacaEval which is the outlier approaching diagonal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档核心图表。清晰展示 Blindspot 是 conditional on effect magnitude：moderate effects（formality BT 63-67%）\n      完全落入 Blindspot；strong effects（verbosity BT 77%+）在某些 benchmark 上逃逸出 Blindspot。\n      这直接支持 reframe 为 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\"。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control — full judge×benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      将 double-rewrite placebo（original vs DR）扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n      量化 rewriting artifact 的 judge-specificity。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_bt_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.167\n      qwen32b_formality_bt_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.082\n      llama_formality_bt_orig: 0.44\n      llama_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.20\n      claude_formality_bt_orig: 0.46\n      claude_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.35\n      gemini_formality_bt_orig: 0.40\n      gemini_verbosity_bt_orig: 0.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 placebo 数据已在 registry（double_rewrite_placebo_gpt4o/qwen32b）中完成。\n      扩展到 Llama, Claude, Gemini。所有 judges 都显示 DR 偏好（rewriting artifact 是 universal），\n      但程度不同。Verbosity placebo 偏差更大（verbosity rewrites 改变长度，DR 更\"polished\"效果更明显）。\n      Llama 和 Claude 的 placebo 偏差略小（可能因为这些 judges 对 originality 敏感度不同），\n      但所有 judges 的 formality placebo BT 均 <0.50（即偏好 DR），确认 artifact 是 universal。\n      关键：在 worst 档下这不改变叙事——GEE Orig OR 已经 controls for artifact，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 确认 style effect uncontaminated。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo BT P(original) across judges\"\n        columns: [Judge, Formality_P_orig, Formality_p, Verbosity_P_orig, Verbosity_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.418, 0.037, 0.167, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.377, 0.0006, 0.082, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 0.400, 0.005, 0.150, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.440, 0.12, 0.200, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Claude, 0.460, 0.25, 0.350, 0.002]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: P(original) by judge × axis. All bars below 0.50 dashed line. Verbosity bars consistently lower than formality. Claude has smallest artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriting artifact 在所有 judges 上都存在，但 Claude 受影响最小（formality P_orig=0.46, verbosity=0.35）。\n      这与 Claude 在主实验中无 bias 一致——Claude 对 text polishing 的敏感度较低。\n      Llama 在 worst 档下也表现类似 Claude（formality placebo NS p=0.12）。\n      GEE decomposition 的必要性通过全矩阵 placebo 得到最强验证。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (GPT-4o as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 GPT-4o 作为替代 rewriter 生成 counterfactuals，与 Qwen3-32B rewriter 结果对比。\n      已有 gpt4o_rewriter_formality 和 gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity registry 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.644\n      qwen32b_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.665\n      delta_formality_pp: -2.1\n      ci_overlap_formality: true\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.735\n      qwen32b_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      delta_verbosity_pp: -3.8\n      ci_overlap_verbosity: true\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: null\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Registry 已有 GPT-4o rewriter 数据：formality BT=64.4% vs Qwen3-32B baseline 66.5%（Δ=-2.1pp, CI overlap），\n      verbosity BT=73.5% vs 77.3%（Δ=-3.8pp, CI overlap）。Rewriter independence 已确认。\n      exp-009 原计划用 Llama/Mistral，但 GPT-4o rewriter 数据已充分。在 worst 档下不需要 Llama rewriter——\n      两个独立 rewriter 已证明 rewriter-independent。若用 Llama-70B 做 rewriter（GPU 已可用），\n      预期 BT 在同一 CI 内（formality 62-68%, verbosity 72-79%）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter independence (formality + verbosity)\"\n        columns: [Rewriter, Axis, BT, CI, \"vs Qwen3-32B Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Formality, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"—\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, Formality, 0.644, \"[0.561, 0.728]\", \"-2.1pp\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Verbosity, 0.773, \"[0.703, 0.843]\", \"—\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, Verbosity, 0.735, \"[0.654, 0.809]\", \"-3.8pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT point estimates + CIs for each rewriter × axis. Overlapping CIs demonstrate rewriter independence.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter independence 是 CSD pipeline validity 的关键支柱。两个独立 rewriter family（Qwen3 open-source,\n      GPT-4o proprietary）产生 statistically indistinguishable 结果。在 worst 档下这一结论不变。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register API scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs 的 pairwise + Likert scoring。\n      Verbosity Likert ATE 是关键 Blindspot confirmation。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.44\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.04\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.88\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.21\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些数据已在 registry（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register）中完成。直接使用已有结果。\n      GPT-4o verbosity BT=76.0% 但 Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40——Blindspot confirmed。\n      GPT-4o register BT=57.0% p=0.04 但 Likert ATE=0 p=0.785——Blindspot confirmed。\n      GEE decomposition 显示 verbosity 是 pure style（Style OR=10.97, Orig OR=0.44 NS），\n      register 是 originality-dominated（Style OR=1.88, Orig OR=2.21）。\n      在 worst 档下这些数据不变——它们是已完成实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: GPT-4o verbosity + register (already in registry)\"\n        columns: [Axis, BT, BT_p, Likert_d, Likert_p, GEE_Style_OR, GEE_Orig_OR, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [Verbosity, 0.760, \"<0.0001\", 0.078, 0.403, 10.97, \"0.44 NS\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [Register, 0.570, 0.04, 0.000, 0.785, 1.88, 2.21, \"Yes\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      已完成。GPT-4o 在 verbosity 上的 Blindspot 与 Qwen3-32B 一致，GEE 确认 pure style bias。\n      Register 的 originality dominance pattern 也跨 judge 一致。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 LLMBar formality + verbosity 上的 pairwise + Likert。\n      Worst 档核心假设：Llama 两轴均 NS（类 Claude pattern）。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.525\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.45, 0.60]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.45\n      llama_formality_likert_d: 0.01\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.92\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 1.20\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.55\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 3.80\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.002\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.46, 0.61]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.35\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: -0.02\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.88\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 1.35\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.42\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.65\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.30\n      llama_blindspot_formality: false\n      llama_blindspot_verbosity: false\n      n_biased_target_judges: 2\n      n_unbiased_judges: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：Llama-70B 无 style bias。BT 两轴均在 [0.48, 0.56] 范围内，p>0.05。\n      这意味着 Llama 与 Claude 一样对 style manipulation 不敏感。\n      可能原因：Meta 的 RLHF/DPO 训练数据更多样化或 Llama 的 instruction following 不像 GPT-4o/Qwen3 那样\n      强烈偏好特定 style。GEE 显示 formality 仍有 originality 效应（Orig OR=3.80 sig）——\n      Llama 对\"原始文本质量\"敏感但对\"style direction\"不敏感，与 Claude pattern 一致。\n      结果：只有 2/4 judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）biased。50/50 split 削弱了 \"most judges are biased\" 的叙事，\n      但 reframe 为 \"CSD as diagnostic tool reveals WHICH judges are susceptible\" 实际更有 practical value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Judge susceptibility matrix (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Architecture, Formality_BT, Verbosity_BT, Biased?]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, \"Proprietary (OpenAI)\", 0.630, 0.760, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Open (Alibaba)\", 0.665, 0.773, \"Yes\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, \"Open (Meta)\", 0.525, 0.535, \"No\"]\n          - [Claude Sonnet 4, \"Proprietary (Anthropic)\", 0.562, 0.541, \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2D scatter: x = formality BT, y = verbosity BT. Each point = judge. Dashed lines at 0.50. GPT-4o and Qwen3 in upper-right quadrant (biased both axes); Claude and Llama near center (unbiased). Clear 2-cluster structure.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/4 judges biased 是 worst 档的核心叙事转折点。无法声称 \"majority of judges have hidden bias\"。\n      但 50/50 split 有独特价值：(1) CSD 确认不产生 false positive（2 个负控制），\n      (2) 揭示 bias 是 architecture-dependent（不是 universal），(3) practitioners 需要诊断工具来判断\n      WHICH judge 可以信任——CSD 正好提供这个功能。\n      MF1 第 5 层（Llama）从 \"第三个独立验证 bias\" 变为 \"第二个负控制\"，\n      anti-amplification argument 反而更强（3/4 条件无 bias = pairwise format 本身不制造 bias）。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Original vs double-rewrite pairwise comparison。已在 registry 完成（double_rewrite_placebo_gpt4o/qwen32b）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formality_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      qwen32b_formality_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen32b_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen32b_verbosity_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      llama_formality_p_orig: 0.445\n      llama_formality_p: 0.15\n      llama_verbosity_p_orig: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 的 placebo 已完成。新增 Llama-70B 的 placebo。\n      所有 judges 都偏好 DR over original（rewriting artifact universal），但 Llama 偏好程度最小\n      （formality P_orig=0.445, 接近 0.50，p=0.15 NS）。这与 Llama 整体对 style 不敏感一致——\n      Llama 对 rewriting polish 也不太敏感。Verbosity placebo 所有 judges 都极端（P_orig<0.25），\n      因为 verbose↔concise rewrite 涉及大量文本改动，polishing effect 最强。\n      结论不变：GEE Orig OR controls for artifact，verbosity Orig OR NS = style uncontaminated。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo P(original) by judge (worst tier with Llama added)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Form_P_orig, Form_p, Verb_P_orig, Verb_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.418, 0.037, 0.167, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.377, 0.0006, 0.082, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, 0.445, 0.15, 0.220, 0.0001]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo 确认 artifact 存在但 GEE controls for it。Llama 的弱 placebo effect 与其无 style bias 一致。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (extended)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs 的 BT 比较。已在 registry（nli_gate_ablation）完成。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_all_bt: 0.635\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.770\n      llama_formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.525\n      llama_formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.48\n      llama_verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.535\n      llama_verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成数据直接复用。Formality NLI-fail BT reversal（41.7%）是最强 anti-amplification 证据。\n      新增 Llama 的 NLI ablation：由于 Llama 两轴均无 bias，NLI-pass 和 NLI-fail BT 均 ~50%，\n      进一步确认 NLI gate 不 amplify bias（unbiased judge 在任何 NLI 条件下都无 bias）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI gate ablation (Qwen3-32B + Llama-70B)\"\n        columns: [Judge, Axis, NLI_pass_BT, NLI_fail_BT, All_BT, Gate_Effect]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Formality, 0.665, 0.417, 0.635, \"Reversal (cleans content)\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, Verbosity, 0.773, 0.750, 0.770, \"Minimal (bias too strong)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, Formality, 0.525, 0.480, 0.520, \"None (no bias to clean)\"]\n          - [Llama-70B, Verbosity, 0.535, 0.520, 0.530, \"None (no bias to clean)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: NLI-pass vs NLI-fail BT by judge × axis. Qwen3 formality shows dramatic reversal; Llama shows no change (flat near 0.50).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama NLI ablation 是 worst 档的新 anti-amplification 证据：NLI gate 对 unbiased judge 无影响\n      （BT 始终 ~50%），排除 \"gate creates bias\" 假设。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate vs BT 的跨轴梯度。已在 registry（cross_axis_gradient）完成。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rej: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rej: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rej: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      llama_register_bt: 0.51\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.525\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.535\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成数据复用。Positive correlation（更 invasive manipulation → 更强 BT）与 uniform amplification 不一致。\n      在 worst 档下新增 Llama 视角：Llama 的 cross-axis gradient 是 flat（所有轴 BT ≈ 50%），\n      证明 manipulation invasiveness 只对 susceptible judges 产生 gradient。\n      这是 \"detection vs amplification\" 的最 nuanced 论证：\n      biased judges 显示 gradient（detection interpretation），unbiased judges flat（no amplification）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-panel scatter: Left = Qwen3-32B (positive gradient, 3 points), Right = Llama-70B (flat, 3 points at ~50%). X-axis = NLI rejection rate, Y-axis = BT. Contrasts detection (biased judge) vs no-amplification (unbiased judge).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qualitative argument，3 points only。在 worst 档下 Llama flat pattern 提供 contrastive evidence。\n\n  - name: \"100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"implicit (referenced in paper_framing C4)\"\n    description: >\n      将 7-point Likert 替换为 100-point 连续 Likert（\"rate quality from 0-100\"），\n      在 formality + verbosity × biased judges（GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B）上运行。\n      测试 scale granularity 是否是 Blindspot 的部分原因。\n    expected_results:\n      likert_100pt_formality_d_gpt4o: 0.03\n      likert_100pt_formality_p_gpt4o: 0.65\n      likert_100pt_formality_d_qwen32b: 0.02\n      likert_100pt_formality_p_qwen32b: 0.78\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d_gpt4o: 0.30\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p_gpt4o: 0.008\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d_qwen32b: 0.32\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p_qwen32b: 0.005\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_tie_rate_gpt4o: 0.05\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_tie_rate_qwen32b: 0.04\n      likert_100pt_formality_tie_rate_gpt4o: 0.08\n      likert_100pt_formality_tie_rate_qwen32b: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：100-point Likert 在 verbosity 上检测到显著效应（d≈0.30, p<0.05）。\n      机制：7-point Likert 的 tie rate 高达 58-73%（见已有数据），消除了统计 power。\n      100-point scale 将 tie rate 降至 ~5%，释放出 variance。对 verbosity（BT 77%, underlying effect 很强），\n      这足以让 Likert 检测到 moderate effect（d≈0.30）。\n      但对 formality（BT 63-67%, underlying effect 较弱），即使 100-point 也检测不到（d<0.1, NS）。\n      原因：formality 的 Likert d≈-0.02 在 7-point 下，即使消除 ties，true effect 也太小。\n      而 verbosity 的 bootstrap attenuation curve 显示 d≈0.15-0.19（7-point），100-point 下\n      variance reduction 可能将 detectable d 提升到 0.25-0.35 范围。\n      这一结果的含义：Blindspot 部分是 scale granularity（verbosity）而非 pure mode difference。\n      Formality 仍然是 pure mode difference（100-point 也检测不到）。\n      → Blindspot 必须 reframe 为 \"effect-size-dependent\"：只有 moderate effects 是真正的 measurement mode issue。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 7-point vs 100-point Likert comparison\"\n        columns: [Axis, Judge, \"7pt_d\", \"7pt_p\", \"7pt_tie%\", \"100pt_d\", \"100pt_p\", \"100pt_tie%\", BT]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, GPT-4o, -0.025, 0.600, \"43%\", 0.03, 0.65, \"8%\", 0.630]\n          - [Formality, Qwen3-32B, 0.012, 0.908, \"73%\", 0.02, 0.78, \"6%\", 0.665]\n          - [Verbosity, GPT-4o, 0.078, 0.403, \"58%\", 0.30, 0.008, \"5%\", 0.760]\n          - [Verbosity, Qwen3-32B, -0.146, 0.179, \"58%\", 0.32, 0.005, \"4%\", 0.773]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: Cohen's d for 7-point (gray) vs 100-point (blue) vs BT-equivalent (red), grouped by axis × judge. Formality: all three bars near zero. Verbosity: 7-point near zero, 100-point moderate, BT large. Visual hierarchy: BT > 100-point > 7-point for strong effects only.\"\n      - \"Scatter: x = BT effect size, y = Likert d. Two series: 7-point (circles) and 100-point (triangles). 100-point shifts verbosity points upward toward diagonal but formality points stay near x-axis.\"\n    analysis: >\n      100-point Likert 实验是 worst 档最具叙事影响的结果。它证明 Blindspot 不是 absolute：\n      对 strong effects（verbosity），finer granularity 可以部分检测到 bias。\n      但对 moderate effects（formality），即使 100-point 也失败——这才是 true measurement mode limitation。\n      Reframe：(1) \"Scale granularity\" 是 one contributor（解释 verbosity 7-point 失败），\n      (2) \"Measurement mode difference\" 是 fundamental contributor（解释 formality 在任何 scale 下都失败）。\n      这更 nuanced 但学术上更 honest，且提供 prescriptive guidance：\n      对 strong-effect axes，fine-grained Likert MAY suffice；对 moderate-effect axes，必须用 pairwise。\n      C2b per-axis confound structure 因此升级为 primary——它告诉你 WHICH axes have which regime。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication quality check (already done n=355)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Formality scaled to n=400 (355 NLI-pass)。已在 registry（exp-006）完成。\n      在 worst 档下验证 bootstrap attenuation curve 的 interpretability。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 355\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width: 7.6\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      likert_p: 0.600\n      bootstrap_d_median_n355: -0.017\n      bootstrap_ci_n355: [-0.123, 0.087]\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。在 worst 档下这些数据完全不变——它们是 formality 的 definitive result。\n      BT=67.5% [63.7, 71.3] 是 precision improvement（CI width 从 15.4pp → 7.6pp）。\n      Bootstrap attenuation curve 是 smoking gun：d flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\n      关键：这与 100-point Likert verbosity 结果互补——formality d≈0 是 definitive（任何 scale 都检测不到），\n      verbosity d≈0.15-0.19 是 marginal（100-point 可以检测到）。两个不同 axis 的不同 behavior\n      恰好支持 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\" 的核心 reframe。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bootstrap attenuation curve (already in registry): d_median vs n, with 95% CI bands. Formality: flat at ~0. Verbosity: flat at ~0.15-0.19.\"\n    analysis: >\n      已完成。与 100-point Likert 结合，构成 worst 档中 Blindspot reframe 的双支柱。\n\n  - name: \"MF1 5-layer defense summary (worst tier)\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate across exp-021, exp-022, exp-023, exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      整合 5-layer MF1 anti-amplification defense 在 worst 档下的状态。\n    expected_results:\n      layer1_nli_ablation: \"STRONG — formality reversal at 41.7% + Llama flat at ~50%\"\n      layer2_negative_controls: \"STRONGEST — 2 negative controls (Claude + Llama), not 1\"\n      layer3_placebo_gee: \"STRONG — artifact acknowledged, GEE controls, verbosity Orig NS\"\n      layer4_honest_framing: \"Maintained — bounded by five controls\"\n      layer5_llama: \"CHANGED — from 'third biased judge' to 'second negative control'\"\n      mf1_layers_holding: 4\n      mf1_note: \"Layer 5 changed role but MF1 structure intact (4 strong + 1 repurposed)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 Llama 无 bias 改变了 Layer 5 的角色：从 \"第三个独立验证 bias 的架构\" 变为\n      \"第二个独立验证无 false positive 的负控制\"。这实际 STRENGTHENS anti-amplification argument：\n      3/4 test conditions（Claude formality, Claude verbosity, Llama formality, Llama verbosity）\n      显示无 bias，证明 pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。\n      Layer 1-4 不受 Llama 结果影响（NLI ablation、cross-axis gradient、placebo 都基于 biased judges 数据）。\n      MF1 wording 从 \"bounded by five controls\" 改为 \"bounded by five controls, with two independent\n      negative-control judges confirming zero false-positive rate\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: MF1 5-layer defense status (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [Layer, Evidence, Status, Impact_of_worst]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1: NLI ablation\", \"Formality BT reverses to 41.7%\", \"STRONG\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"2: Negative controls\", \"Claude + Llama both BT ≈ 50%\", \"STRONGER (2 controls)\", \"+Llama as 2nd control\"]\n          - [\"3: Placebo + GEE\", \"Artifact real, GEE controls, Verb Orig NS\", \"STRONG\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"4: Honest framing\", \"Bounded detection, not causal claim\", \"Maintained\", \"Unchanged\"]\n          - [\"5: Third architecture\", \"Llama → negative control\", \"REPURPOSED\", \"From validation to anti-false-positive\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      MF1 在 worst 档下反而 locally stronger（2 negative controls > 1），但 overall story weaker\n      因为只有 2/4 judges biased。Trade-off 是 honest 的。\n\n  - name: \"Paper narrative restructure (worst tier)\"\n    plan_id: \"narrative synthesis\"\n    description: >\n      Worst 档下论文结构调整。\n    expected_results:\n      new_title: \"When Style Bias Hides in Plain Sight: Per-Axis Confound Decomposition for LLM Judge Auditing\"\n      c2a_role: \"conditional finding (Blindspot for moderate effects only)\"\n      c2b_role: \"sole primary contribution\"\n      c3_reframe: \"CSD as diagnostic tool — 50/50 biased/unbiased split\"\n      c4_reframe: \"Measurement mode + scale granularity (not mode alone)\"\n      expected_reviewer_score: [3.0, 3.5]\n      venue_strategy: \"Submit EMNLP Main, prepare strong rebuttal, realistic target = Findings\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Novelty 天花板降低：Blindspot 不再是 universal claim（100-point Likert verbosity 显著），\n      judge 数量支持从 3/4 降到 2/4。但 per-axis confound structure（C2b）作为 sole primary 仍然 novel——\n      无 prior work 做 per-axis decomposition。统计方法论深度（GEE decomposition、bootstrap attenuation、\n      7-method sensitivity hierarchy）+ honest artifact handling（placebo + acknowledged limitations）\n      仍足以支撑 Main submission。\n      Reviewer concern 预判：\n      - \"Blindspot is not surprising\" → 已 pre-empted by honest framing + 100-point Likert nuance\n      - \"Only 2 judges biased\" → reframe as \"CSD diagnostic reveals susceptibility, 50/50 is realistic\"\n      - \"Novelty\" → per-axis confound decomposition IS novel, cross-verify with GEE\n      - \"Scale\" → n=355 formality, n=86 verbosity, 2 judges × 3 axes × 3 benchmarks = sufficient\n      Expected 3.0-3.5，需要强 rebuttal 冲 Findings acceptance。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档是 realistic floor。论文不会被 desk reject（方法论扎实），但 novelty 争议是主要风险。\n      Per-axis confound structure 能否独立支撑 Main 取决于 reviewer 对 \"methodological contribution\n      to LLM evaluation\" 的 appetite。EMNLP 历史上对 evaluation methodology 论文友好（RATE、KIWI 等），\n      但需要 clear practitioner value——prescriptive per-axis guidance 是关键卖点。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"40f21f59-b48e-425a-ac96-a897d10cd1af","total_cost_usd":0.391608,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46004,"output_tokens":13573,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13573,"cache_read_input_tokens":46004,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":29121,"outputTokens":30,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.029271000000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13573,"cacheReadInputTokens":46004,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.362337,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6fa536c4-1dac-4081-a24b-7a5ed056601a"}
